pySMESH: CompositeHexa_3D refuses viscous layers instead of crashing (SMESH V9_16_0).

Defect: CompositeHexa_3D with a ViscousLayers hypothesis on its solid ends the process with an
access violation.

Symptom: the unit box, Regular_1D with 4 segments, Quadrangle_2D, CompositeHexa_3D and
ViscousLayers (0.3 thick, 3 layers, factor 1.2) on one face, all assigned to a compound root
holding the box (as pySMESH loads a shape): the compute crashes. On a bare SOLID, SMESH
refuses the hypothesis at assignment (HYP_INCOMPATIBLE), so Compute never sees it.

Root cause, measured with instrumented builds: Compute takes the hypothesis by name
(StdMeshers_CompositeHexa_3D.cxx:858-859) and calls StdMeshers_ViscousLayers::Compute (:862).
The layer builder takes its hypotheses from the algorithm's used hypotheses, filtered by the
compatible list (StdMeshers_ViscousLayers.cxx:2153-2215), and CompositeHexa_3D lists none, so
the builder fails with "ViscousLayers hypothesis not found". StdMeshers_ViscousLayers::Compute
then returns a null proxy mesh and drops that error (:1347-1349), and Compute dereferences the
null pointer (:872). Listing ViscousLayers as compatible builds the layers, but the layer
quadrangles on the four side faces give their grids more rows than the opposite faces have,
and the box grid then holds null nodes (16 of 200 on the probe box): the compute crashes
later. Supporting the layers needs a face-grid loader that leaves the layer cells out.

Change, in StdMeshers_CompositeHexa_3D.cxx only: when a ViscousLayers hypothesis applies,
Compute returns COMPERR_BAD_PARMETERS, "CompositeHexa_3D does not build viscous layers;
Hexa_3D does", before any layer is built.

Not changed: CompositeHexa_3D with no ViscousLayers hypothesis.
diff --git a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_CompositeHexa_3D.cxx b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_CompositeHexa_3D.cxx
--- a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_CompositeHexa_3D.cxx
+++ b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_CompositeHexa_3D.cxx
@@ -859,9 +859,13 @@
   const SMESH_Hypothesis *          hyp = theMesh.GetHypothesis( theShape, vlFilter, true );
   const StdMeshers_ViscousLayers* vlHyp = static_cast< const StdMeshers_ViscousLayers* >( hyp );
   if ( vlHyp )
-    proxyMesh = vlHyp->Compute( theMesh, theShape, /*toMakeN2NMap=*/true );
-  else
-    proxyMesh.reset( new SMESH_ProxyMesh( theMesh ));
+    // pySMESH: the layers fail here (the hypothesis is not among the compatible ones, so
+    // the builder does not find it), and Compute then read a null proxy mesh and crashed.
+    // Made compatible, the layer quadrangles on the side FACEs give the side grids more
+    // rows than the opposite FACEs have, and the box grid gets null nodes. Refuse it.
+    return error( COMPERR_BAD_PARMETERS,
+                  "CompositeHexa_3D does not build viscous layers; Hexa_3D does" );
+  proxyMesh.reset( new SMESH_ProxyMesh( theMesh ));
 
